.\" Generated by docs/reference/generate-man.py from cps --help.
.TH "CPS-INSTALL" 1 "" "CPS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&cps\-install \- \&Install packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP 4
.B \&cps install [OPTIONS] [PACKAGE]...
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B \&[PACKAGE]...
\&Packages to install, optionally with a publisher and version
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \&\-\-root <IMAGE>
\&Operate on this offline image instead of the running system
.TP
.B \&\-\-config <CONFIG>
\&Distribution configuration of the running system [default: /etc/cps/image.kdl]
.TP
.B \&\-y, \-\-yes
\&Confirm the displayed transaction without prompting
.TP
.B \&\-n, \-\-dry\-run
\&Preview the transaction without applying it
.TP
.B \&\-\-save\-plan <PLAN>
\&Save the exact transaction plan, for `cps status \-\-plan` or a later `cps apply`
.TP
.B \&\-\-no\-recommends
\&Skip recommended packages when resolving the transaction
.TP
.B \&\-\-no\-refresh
\&Use the currently cached catalogs (images always plan from their cache)
.TP
.B \&\-\-stage
\&Stage the change in a new Btrfs trial boot environment, or for repair and revert a verified recovery root, instead of changing the running root
.TP
.B \&\-\-exact
\&Reconcile the image to exactly these packages and their dependencies
.TP
.B \&\-\-profile
\&Install the configured signed release profile into an image with no packages
.TP
.B \&\-\-lock <LOCK>
\&Install the exact composition of this image lock into a newly created image
.TP
.B \&\-\-git <GIT>
\&Build and install the package described by cps.kdl in this Git repository
.TP
.B \&\-\-commit <COMMIT>
\&Pin the Git install to a full commit ID
.TP
.B \&\-\-track\-branch <TRACK_BRANCH>
\&Follow this branch when running cps upgrade
.TP
.B \&\-\-allowed\-signers <FORMAT:PATH>
\&Require Git signatures from the signers in ssh:PATH or openpgp:PATH
.TP
.B \&\-\-require\-signed <REQUIRE_SIGNED>
\&Which Git object must carry the allowed signature Possible values: \- commit: The installed commit itself \- tag:    An annotated tag that points at the installed commit [default: commit]
.TP
.B \&\-h, \-\-help
\&Print help (see a summary with '\-h')
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cps (1)
